WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.679
Somewhere on a network you can't trust,
something is moving.

2
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:15.716
It starts from a USB stick. Nothing is
installed. Nothing is left behind.

3
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.402
Firmware, kernel, the Phoenix splash, then
your desktop.

4
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:30.236
The first boot asks for a name and an
account, then gets out of your way.

5
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.194
A cyberdeck built for your three a.m.
self.

6
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.469
Every tool, one menu.

7a
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.869
The Orion Cockpit lets you see, and hear,

7b
00:00:47.869 --> 00:00:51.801
the network around you. Every detection
lands on one event bus.

8a
00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.670
Producers publish once. Rain sounds it.

8b
00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:01.656
The Cockpit shows it. What you hear and
what you see always agree.

9
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.901
Decks find each other and form an
encrypted WireGuard mesh.

10
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.676
Every deck peers with every other. No hub.
No cloud.

11
00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.214
Team chat runs over that mesh, on your own
Matrix server.

12
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:35.322
Threat posture comes in three tiers, from
quiet watching to decoys and canaries.

13a
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.946
When an alert is your own scanner, squelch
it for thirty minutes or tune it for good,

13b
00:01:41.946 --> 00:01:44.856
and the deck tells you whether that
survives a reboot.

14
00:01:52.256 --> 00:01:55.592
Packet captures, memory images, suspicious
binaries.

15
00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:01.997
Wireshark. Volatility. YARA. capa.

16
00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:05.725
Offline. On the stick.

17
00:02:13.756 --> 00:02:18.783
Nebula is a local AI copilot. Its model is
hash-checked at every boot.

18a
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.582
Its tools can look, but they cannot

18b
00:02:21.582 --> 00:02:24.153
improvise commands. Nothing leaves the
deck.

19
00:02:28.983 --> 00:02:31.854
The Orion Workbench is the analyst's
toolbox.

20
00:02:34.483 --> 00:02:37.433
God's Eye will not reach out until the
deck says it can.

21
00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:41.012
CyberChef decodes.

22
00:02:42.983 --> 00:02:47.325
And Pivotglass keeps hypotheses, evidence
and contradictions apart.

23
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:52.949
Monitor. Detect. Defend. Triage. Timeline.
One stick.

24
00:02:58.483 --> 00:03:02.957
Orion X, Phoenix Edition. A cyberdeck for
the good guys. All of them.
